# T-1016: Documents runtime behavior of a dict that COULD satisfy a {host: String _ : Int}
# column constraint. The column constraint annotation syntax itself is not exercised here —
# the {host: String _ : Int} type annotation form is handled by resolve_type_dict only
# when used in a [let x@[host: String _ : Int]] parameter annotation. This test covers
# the eval-level behavior: dict construction with a String-typed host field and Int-typed
# remaining fields (port, timeout), and field access via dot notation.
# Absence of === warn asserts no type warnings from the structural access chain.
[
  config: [host: "localhost"  port: 8080  timeout: 30]
  result: config.port
]
=== out
Dict({"config": Dict({"host": String("localhost"), "port": Int(8080), "timeout": Int(30)}), "result": Int(8080)})
